{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "op": "ANSWER",
      "refs": ["net_new_mrr_trend", "cumulative_mrr_trend", "net_new_mrr_current_state"],
      "text": "Monthly net new MRR has been moving $finding:net_new_mrr_trend.direction across 2024, gaining roughly $finding:net_new_mrr_trend.slope_per_period per month on an OLS fit, while the cumulative MRR base has trended $finding:cumulative_mrr_trend.direction at $finding:cumulative_mrr_trend.slope_per_period per period — meaning the business is not merely holding ground but compounding it. The most recent complete month came in at $finding:net_new_mrr_current_state.latest_value ($finding:net_new_mrr_current_state.latest_period), sitting $finding:net_new_mrr_current_state.pct_from_peak off the $finding:net_new_mrr_current_state.peak_period peak of $finding:net_new_mrr_current_state.peak_value."
    },
    {
      "op": "EXPLAIN",
      "refs": ["net_new_mrr_trend", "cumulative_mrr_trend", "net_new_mrr_current_state", "net_new_mrr_peak", "net_new_mrr_trough"],
      "anchor": "chart_mrr_over_time",
      "text": "The chart below traces both the month-by-month net new MRR and its running cumulative sum through 2024. The monthly series swings between a trough of $finding:net_new_mrr_trough.value in $finding:net_new_mrr_trough.period and a peak of $finding:net_new_mrr_peak.value in $finding:net_new_mrr_peak.period — a spread that reflects real variation in the mix of new business, expansion, and churn rather than any detected structural break. The cumulative line's steady $finding:cumulative_mrr_trend.direction slope is the cleaner read on momentum: month-to-month noise averages out, and the compounding effect is visible."
    },
    {
      "op": "VIEW",
      "component": "DualAxisChart",
      "series": "mrr_over_time",
      "text": "Net New MRR and Cumulative MRR over time (2024)"
    },
    {
      "op": "TREND",
      "refs": ["new_mrr_trend", "expansion_mrr_trend", "churn_mrr_trend", "mrr_annual_decomposition"],
      "text": "Breaking the headline figure into its drivers: new MRR has trended $finding:new_mrr_trend.direction at $finding:new_mrr_trend.slope_per_period per month, while expansion has moved $finding:expansion_mrr_trend.direction at $finding:expansion_mrr_trend.slope_per_period — together they represent the growth engine. Churn has trended $finding:churn_mrr_trend.direction at $finding:churn_mrr_trend.slope_per_period per month, which is the drag to watch. Across the full year, the dominant annual contributor is $finding:mrr_annual_decomposition.dominant, with new MRR summing to $finding:mrr_annual_decomposition.new_mrr_contribution, expansion adding $finding:mrr_annual_decomposition.expansion_mrr_contribution, and churn subtracting $finding:mrr_annual_decomposition.churn_mrr_drag — and because these three components fully account for net MRR, no residual is unexplained."
    },
    {
      "op": "CONTRAST",
      "refs": ["net_new_mrr_split_comparison"],
      "text": "Splitting 2024 at its midpoint reinforces the directional story: the first half ($finding:net_new_mrr_split_comparison.early_span, n=$finding:net_new_mrr_split_comparison.early_n months) carried a median net new MRR of $finding:net_new_mrr_split_comparison.early_median, while the second half ($finding:net_new_mrr_split_comparison.late_span, n=$finding:net_new_mrr_split_comparison.late_n months) ran at $finding:net_new_mrr_split_comparison.late_median — a $finding:net_new_mrr_split_comparison.multiplier multiple, indicating the back half of the year meaningfully outpaced the front."
    },
    {
      "op": "NOTE",
      "refs": ["net_new_mrr_step_change"],
      "text": "No persistent step change in monthly net new MRR survived the detection gates — the variation visible in the monthly series reflects continuous fluctuation rather than a single discrete structural shift."
    },
    {
      "op": "EXPLAIN",
      "refs": ["segment_heterogeneity"],
      "anchor": "chart_mrr_by_plan",
      "text": "The plan-level heatmap below shows how net new MRR distributes across Enterprise, Pro, and Starter through the year. The heterogeneity test ($finding:segment_heterogeneity.test, p=$finding:segment_heterogeneity.p_value) confirms that the three plans differ significantly in their net new MRR levels — the aggregate trend described above is not uniform across segments, and the heatmap's color gradient will reveal which plan drove which months."
    },
    {
      "op": "CALLOUT",
      "refs": ["segment_heterogeneity", "churn_mrr_trend"],
      "text": "The combination of statistically significant plan-level divergence and a $finding:churn_mrr_trend.direction churn trend is the most actionable signal in this dataset: if churn is concentrating in one plan tier, the aggregate slope understates the risk to that segment. The plan heatmap is the right place to look next."
    },
    {
      "op": "METHOD",
      "refs": ["grain_check", "net_new_mrr_trend", "cumulative_mrr_trend", "net_new_mrr_split_comparison", "segment_heterogeneity"],
      "text": "All trends use OLS direction fits over the full 2024 observation window ($finding:grain_check.months months × $finding:grain_check.plans plans = $finding:grain_check.rows rows, one row per plan per month); the half-year comparison uses a midpoint-pinned median split; plan-level significance was tested with $finding:segment_heterogeneity.test dispatch. All MRR component columns were confirmed non-null before analysis."
    },
    {
      "op": "CAVEAT",
      "refs": ["mrr_null_check"],
      "anchor": "chart_mrr_over_time"
    },
    {
      "op": "CONCLUSION",
      "refs": ["net_new_mrr_trend", "net_new_mrr_current_state", "net_new_mrr_split_comparison", "mrr_annual_decomposition"],
      "text": "MRR is on a $finding:net_new_mrr_trend.direction trajectory through 2024: net new MRR is climbing at $finding:net_new_mrr_trend.slope_per_period per month, the second half of the year ran at $finding:net_new_mrr_split_comparison.multiplier the first-half median, and the year's dominant driver is $finding:mrr_annual_decomposition.dominant. At $finding:net_new_mrr_current_state.latest_value in $finding:net_new_mrr_current_state.latest_period, the business is $finding:net_new_mrr_current_state.pct_from_peak off peak — still within striking distance of its best month."
    }
  ]
}
